{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032260-movie-transcendence","id":1032260,"title":"Movie: Transcendence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-15T12:06:38-08:00","id":1032260,"title":"Movie: Transcendence","content":"Has anybody adapted something like this to the nWoD - something like a dying mortal turned into a fawed A.I.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","name":"Nin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:13:19-08:00","id":1032262,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen it, but from the synopsis it sounds like a Promethean story from the perspective of the Created's Demiurge(s). Which sounds like a pretty sweet concept for a game, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:24:02-08:00","id":1032264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032260-movie-transcendence?p=1032262#post1032262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen it, but from the synopsis it sounds like a Promethean story from the perspective of the Created's Demiurge(s). Which sounds like a pretty sweet concept for a game, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd work very well in Promethean if there was a Merit or Bestowment that allowed the new being far more access to the prior hosts memories than any of the existing ones currently do.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it might be an okay Deviant. Not super familiar with the themes at work there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:23:20-08:00","id":1032366,"title":"","content":"Ghost-based technology, mayhaps? Ghosts are personalities/identities based upon a (usually) former living human. It would be an easier, more direct method of brain uploading. Now, we know certain circumstances and even technologies can affect more ephemeral beings (Etheric Rounds, for instance). Whose to say &quot;they&quot; didn't stumble upon some Ghost-Machine Interface technology? The running Mainframe would act as Anchor/Fetter for the imprinted Ghost Intelligence, as well as augment data and processing power.<br /> <br /> Of course, the directions you could take this hardly need to be elaborated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T01:10:11-08:00","id":1032538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032260-movie-transcendence?p=1032366#post1032366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost-based technology, mayhaps? Ghosts are personalities/identities based upon a (usually) former living human. It would be an easier, more direct method of brain uploading. Now, we know certain circumstances and even technologies can affect more ephemeral beings (Etheric Rounds, for instance). Whose to say &quot;they&quot; didn't stumble upon some Ghost-Machine Interface technology? The running Mainframe would act as Anchor/Fetter for the imprinted Ghost Intelligence, as well as augment data and processing power.<br /> <br /> Of course, the directions you could take this hardly need to be elaborated.</div> </div> </div> </div> In the first edition, there was a ghost who became a ghost in the machine, merging with the telephone network. <br /> <br /> There was also a breath eater numina that allowed a ghost to replenish essence by doing bashing damage.<br /> <br /> So I'd go with something like he becomes a ghost in the machine, then uses breath eater to take essence from computer users (headaches, tiredness, eye strain) to climb in rank, which increases his technology influence, until he achieves the create technology level, in which case he's a ghostly singularity. <br /> <br /> But of course his technological miracles are paid for in human life force, even though he hasn't really hurt anyone- yet, or has he? <br /> <br /> Presuming that ghosts can increase in rank through essence gathering like a spirit, it hasn't really been discussed yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:28:43-08:00","id":1032586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032260-movie-transcendence?p=1032538#post1032538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the first edition, there was a ghost who became a ghost in the machine, merging with the telephone network.<br /> <br /> There was also a breath eater numina that allowed a ghost to replenish essence by doing bashing damage.<br /> <br /> So I'd go with something like he becomes a ghost in the machine, then uses breath eater to take essence from computer users (headaches, tiredness, eye strain) to climb in rank, which increases his technology influence, until he achieves the create technology level, in which case he's a ghostly singularity.<br /> <br /> But of course his technological miracles are paid for in human life force, even though he hasn't really hurt anyone- yet, or has he?<br /> <br /> Presuming that ghosts can increase in rank through essence gathering like a spirit, it hasn't really been discussed yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it has been stated that Ghosts don't increase in Rank outside the Underworld. Usually. I'm pretty sure &quot;pioneering Ghost-In-The-Machine technology&quot; probably classifies as exceptional enough circumstances to break the basic rules.<br /> <br /> As for Breath-drinking: does it even need to? Ghosts get Essence from being remembered. Given a decent user base and some regular usage, it should be gorged with Essence from all the interaction. Which it could use to improve performance (either via a Technology Influence, or if the machine is using the Ghost's Attributes for processing, by boosting Power (Intelligence) or Finesse (Wits) to mimic &quot;overclocking&quot;). It could even &quot;cheat&quot; a little: Predictive Analysis? Omen Trance. Remote Tracking? Clairvoyance. Etc.<br /> <br /> Just don't give it Blast. That's how the Ghost-Robot Overlords happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}